# Citation metadata for this repository (https://citation-file-format.github.io).
# GitHub reads it from the default branch for the "Cite this repository" button.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the paper that describes the method."
type: software
title: "Cyclic Behavior Type (CBT) Tool"
abstract: >-
  The Cyclic Behavior Type (CBT) Tool is open-source software that estimates
  whether a fine-grained soil responds to cyclic loading more like a sand or
  more like a clay, from the record of a cyclic direct simple shear (CDSS)
  test. For every loading cycle it computes test metrics that describe the
  stress-strain loops, the excess pore pressure and the strain accumulation:
  the maximum excess pore pressure ratio, the ratio of the loop area to the
  area of its convex hull, the cyclic strain increment ratio, and the strain
  accumulation curvature. From these it estimates the cyclic behavior type
  (CBT), from 0 (clay-like) to 1 (sand-like), with ten Bayesian regression
  models that reproduce the judgments of ten analysts who classified 195 CDSS
  tests from the Next Generation Liquefaction (NGL) database. The analyst
  models are combined with equal weights in logit space, and the result is
  reported with its within- and between-analyst uncertainty. The tool is a
  static website: the Python code runs in the web browser with Pyodide, so
  uploaded test files never leave the user's computer. Tests can be uploaded
  as CSV files in any time and stress units, or loaded directly from the NGL
  database through its REST API. Per-cycle results and batch summaries are
  downloaded as CSV files.
